      "mergedPostDetails": "I have trouble with animating my tongue Phys Bone. It won't be moved with a Phys Bone component on it, even with Is Animated set to true.\nIt's being moved & turned on by a blend tree.\nHere are my Phys Bone settings:",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1181] can't animate Phys Bone",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "642e277c02c70809c1ecd61d",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "On further investigation, if I export the animation out of the FBX file into a .anim file... the tongue still works with the .anim file!\nSo it's something different about the animation itself that triggers the bug.\nI do notice in the animation that's working that position, rotation, and scale is animated on every bone in the tongue.  Whereas in the animation that's not working, only position is being animated.\nPerhaps changing position alone isn't kicking phys bones to pick up that a change was made.  However, so far my experiments to that effect haven't worked.\nPossibly whether the bug is triggered or not relates to the exact order things end up in within the .anim file or something like that.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
