      "statusChangeID": "6467ae63bfd6ad090057c328",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "available in future release",
      "value": "Fixed this issue and it will be available in a future release.\n\nThe problem occurred with animating the position of bones which already had a very small local positional value.  This would mainly affect avatars imported as FBX, as those typically have a 1/100th scale resulting in very tiny positional values for the base armature.  The tongue bones were a common case since they were very tiny parts of the avatar and tended to have the smallest values.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "6467aec55209cf096b575112",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5e877e5e60de627e6ba7946a",
        "alias": "Beige Prawn",
        "aliasID": "65c5754bed6eefce4c8097c4",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/ca08ffbc1ab4f7efa44ec8917b2bced9.png",
        "created": "2020-04-03T18:20:14.715Z",
        "name": "Kiro",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "boardID": "58c62f2b3cf8f8367753b2f0",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-05-19T17:15:49.580Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "6467aec55209cf096b575112",
      "mergedPostDetails": "And it is very inconsistent, although I can't pin point the source of the issue so far. Identical setups on different models yield different results.\nDescription:\nIn certain situations bone transforms are animated with rotation and translation being keyed in the clip for normalized time interpolation (i.e. two keys at idx 0 & 1 representing extremes). Then PhysBones component is applied to one of the transformed bones, which causes the translations to be reset upon activation.\nCaveat:\nThis behaviour is very inconsistent between different models despite using identical approaches.\nConsider the following IDs: avtr_7947c18a-0dea-4dcb-baa8-ba4511af8e46 & avtr_dc8604cd-687a-40ec-8f61-245902329bee.\nUsing RShift+F4 (fingerpoint on the right hand, GestureRightWeight mapped) should normally extend the tongue and bend its bones, which happens if the PB component is inactive. Upon its activation the rotations are kept, but all translations revert to the rest position.\nIn contrast to avtr_29f036dc-1fe6-459c-85e0-09b9a57c392a, where LShift+F3 applies the transforms, and RShift+F3 enables the component. With this one no transforms are reset, despite the approach being identical: normalized time mapping and simple component toggling.\nExpected behaviour:\nPhysBones should consistently respect TRS matrix and evaluate it for each solver step when Is Animated property is checked.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1190] Animated bone transforms are reset to rest position upon PhysBones component awake",
